<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dul Madoba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somaliland-campaign-1900-1920">Somaliland campaign (1900–1920)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dul Madoba was fought on 9 August 1913 in British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, when Dervish forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-abdullah-hassan">Mohammed Abdullah Hassan</a> ambushed the newly formed Somaliland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">Camel</a> Constabulary. The British commander, Richard Corfield, was killed along with many of his men. The defeat led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to withdraw to the coast for a time, leaving the Dervishes dominant in the interior.</p></div>
